--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracker 0557. DECISIONS.md's 2026-09-01 ruling (refined same day)
gates the PDF path at roughly 40 pages, decided by a fallback chain rather
than one field, because the flat-cache form-feed signal alone is blind on
about 45% of cached PDFs (`4 708 of 8 590`, SPEC.md's extract-layer entry).

## Actions

1. Check whether Zotero's `indexedPages` field is exposed on the local API
   (unconfirmed as of the ruling -- this is the first thing to settle, and
   may kill the "first choice" tier if it turns out not to be reachable
   from zoteus's vantage point).
2. If reachable, use it as the primary length signal.
3. Else, count literal page-break markers (form-feeds) in the flat
   `/fulltext` cache, where present.
4. Else, estimate page count from character count (an assumed
   chars-per-page ratio) -- last resort, never a hard failure to decide.
5. Threshold: ~40 pages, from the author's acceptance-test statement
   (ticket 0028 log, 2026-09-01). Not separately re-argued for the
   estimated case per the ruling.

## Test

- Three fixtures, one per tier: a document where `indexedPages` is
  available, one where only form-feeds are, one where neither is (forces
  the char-count estimate) -- assert each produces a length decision and
  the correct tier was actually used (not silently a different one).

## Invariants

- The gate always produces a decision; it degrades to an estimate, it does
  not fail to fire.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `indexedPages` local-API reachability settled, one way or the other
- [ ] all three tiers implemented and tested
- [ ] threshold configurable in one place, not hardcoded per call site
